Subject: [PATCH] Depend on suds rather than suds-community

Upstream suds defaults its distribution name to suds-community and lets it be
overridden, and conda-forge builds it as `suds`:

  # Default package name is suds-community and needs to be overridden with an
  # environment variable
  -- conda-forge/suds-feedstock

So nothing on conda-forge installs metadata named suds-community at 1.2.0 or
newer; suds-community is a separate feedstock still at 1.1.2. The module
imports fine either way, but pip check compares names:

  checkmarxpythonsdk 1.9.1 requires suds-community, which is not installed.

--- a/setup.py	2026-10-02 16:38:04
+++ b/setup.py	2026-10-02 16:38:05
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
     python_requires='>=3.9',
     install_requires=[
         "httpx>=0.28.1",
-        "suds-community>=1.2.0",
+        "suds>=1.2.0",
         "Deprecated>=1.2.13,<1.3",
         "inflection>=0.5.1"
     ],
